comment0.target=SlotMachineCoverageTest
comment0.text=\n Coverage tests for the domain package\: error cases and branches of\n SlotMachine, Wheel and SlotMachineContest that the cycle\n tests don't reach. The machine is never made visible, so no message\n dialog is opened.\n\n @author  Oscar Poveda, Elian Ibarra\n @version 1.0\n
comment1.target=SlotMachineCoverageTest()
comment1.text=\n Default constructor for test class SlotMachineCoverageTest\n
comment10.target=void shouldNotBeJackpotWithoutSymbolsOrWithLessThanTwoWheels()
comment10.text=\n Verifies that there's no jackpot without symbols (an error) nor\n with less than two wheels (not an error).\n
comment11.target=void shouldReturnNullForWheelOutOfRange()
comment11.text=\n Verifies that getWheel returns null for positions that don't exist.\n
comment12.target=void shouldDeleteEveryWheel()
comment12.text=\n Verifies that every wheel can be deleted, leaving the machine\n empty, and that deleting from an empty machine fails.\n
comment13.target=void wheelShouldIgnoreDeletingMissingOrLastSymbol()
comment13.text=\n Verifies that a wheel ignores deleting a symbol it doesn't have\n and deleting its last symbol.\n
comment14.target=void wheelShouldKeepTheRightSymbolWhenSymbolsAreDeleted()
comment14.text=\n Verifies that a wheel keeps showing the right symbol when a symbol\n before, after or at its current position is deleted.\n
comment15.target=void wheelWithoutSymbolsShouldNotFail()
comment15.text=\n Verifies that a wheel created without registered symbols can be\n spun and shows no symbol.\n
comment16.target=void wheelsShouldMoveBetweenRows()
comment16.text=\n Verifies that wheels move to the next row when a wheel is inserted\n before the end of a full row, and back to the previous row when a\n wheel before them is deleted.\n
comment17.target=void shouldCreateTheContestSolver()
comment17.text=\n Verifies that the contest solver can be instantiated.\n
comment18.target=void lockedLeftyShouldNotChangeItsSymbols()
comment18.text=\n Verifies that a locked lefty wheel rejects a spin without its symbols\n reacting to it\: an ephemeral symbol doesn't shrink.\n
comment19.target=void lockedLazyShouldRejectEverySpin()
comment19.text=\n Verifies that a locked lazy wheel rejects every spin, even while it is\n asleep, and that the rejected spins don't wake it up.\n
comment2.target=void setUp()
comment2.text=\n Sets up the test fixture.\n\n Called before every test case method.\n
comment3.target=void shouldNotLockMissingOrAlreadyLockedWheel()
comment3.text=\n Verifies that a wheel that doesn't exist or is already locked\n can't be locked.\n
comment4.target=void shouldNotUnlockWithoutWheelsOrMissingWheel()
comment4.text=\n Verifies that unlock fails when the machine has no wheels or the\n wheel doesn't exist.\n
comment5.target=void shouldAddSymbolFirstWhenPositionIsBelowOne()
comment5.text=\n Verifies that a symbol added at a position below 1 is inserted\n first in the catalog.\n
comment6.target=void shouldNotSwapWithoutWheelsOrSameAdjustedWheel()
comment6.text=\n Verifies that swap fails without wheels and when both positions\n end up being the same wheel after being adjusted.\n
comment7.target=void shouldNotSpinAWheelWithoutWheels()
comment7.text=\n Verifies that spinning one wheel, with or without steps, fails\n when the machine has no wheels.\n
comment8.target=void shouldSpinAllExceptLockedWheel()
comment8.text=\n Verifies that spinning all the wheels skips the locked one and\n still spins the others.\n
comment9.target=void shouldNotPlaceSymbolOnLockedWheel()
comment9.text=\n Verifies that a symbol can't be placed on a locked wheel.\n
numComments=20
